Kind: ablation
Issue: #904
Takes out: the shell's close of its copy of each pipe's read end -- ush keeps it, so that once the reader of "/musl_test pipe-yes | /musl_test pipe-head" has gone, a reader is still there: the writer fills the pipe and waits, and its EPIPE never comes
Script: scripts/ush-x86_64.py
Expect: ush-x86_64: '/musl_test pipe-yes \| /musl_test pipe-head' never said 'musl_test \(pipe-yes\): write answered EPIPE

diff --git a/uros/src/cmds/ush/ush.c b/uros/src/cmds/ush/ush.c
index 7f64e84c..bfdd6ada 100644
--- a/uros/src/cmds/ush/ush.c
+++ b/uros/src/cmds/ush/ush.c
@@ -452,8 +452,7 @@ run_pipeline(char **stage[], int n, int bg)
         if (i == 0)
             pgid = pid[0];
         (void)setpgid(pid[i], pgid);
-        if (in >= 0)
-            (void)close(in);
+        /* 904-ush-read-end-kept: the shell keeps its copy of the read end */
         if (fds[1] >= 0)
             (void)close(fds[1]);
         in = fds[0];
